WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:06.870
Speaker 1: OK, let's continue speaking to
folks because people want to chat.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:09.879
That's just the reality of what's going on
right now.

00:00:09.879 --> 00:00:13.150
Let's go next to Chad from Florida.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.720
Hey, David.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.350
Hey, Chad, are you in Florida or Florida?

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.680
Speaker 3: Well, that depends on who you ask.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.810
Speaker 1: OK, fair, OK, good.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:30.030
Speaker 3: So my first question, or maybe
only when we can get to, is do you think the

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:35.750
left has sort of squandered this opportunity
to distance themselves from socialism, making

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:41.260
an issue of the embargoes or the authoritarian
or sorry, not socialism, communism, you know,

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:47.350
making an issue of the embargoes or the authoritarian
aspect of the government, as opposed to saying

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.700
we reject communism.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.070
You know, Bernie Sanders isn't a communist.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.070
He does.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.040
He wants to implement, you know, some sort
of socialized health care.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.820
We're not you know, he doesn't want to be
Cuba.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.440
Speaker 1: No, I don't I don't think so.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.440
Let me see.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:10.979
How can I answer this in sort of the most
clear way, I've seen just about every prominent

00:01:10.979 --> 00:01:19.939
Democrat say that they aren't supportive of
60 plus years of uninterrupted Castro family

00:01:19.939 --> 00:01:22.279
rule in Cuba.

00:01:22.279 --> 00:01:27.249
And at the same time, many of them, although
not all, have made it clear that the embargo

00:01:27.249 --> 00:01:28.820
has been completely counterproductive.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:31.029
And that's that's my position.

00:01:31.029 --> 00:01:36.330
I don't know that there should be this expectation
of denouncing communism.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:40.130
Every time you talk about Cuba just does it
doesn't really make sense to me.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:44.119
I mean, when I talk about it, I just make
it clear I'm a progressive.

00:01:44.119 --> 00:01:49.319
So I don't support authoritarian, autocratic
regimes run by what are effectively dictators

00:01:49.319 --> 00:01:51.119
or at minimum authoritarian strongmen.

00:01:51.119 --> 00:01:55.770
I make that clear because my audience sometimes
gets very confused about what my positions

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:56.959
are on these issues.

00:01:56.959 --> 00:02:00.919
But I don't think it's reasonable to say every
time a Democrat talks about Cuba, they should

00:02:00.919 --> 00:02:02.099
denounce communism.

00:02:02.099 --> 00:02:03.899
That sounds weird to me.

00:02:03.899 --> 00:02:07.439
OK, good answer.

00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:08.450
My pleasure.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:08.780
My pleasure

